n**What the grid contains.** Each input has a short horizontal row of single coloured cells at the top. I'll call this the *legend*: for example `1 3 4` or `2 8 3`. Below it are one or more grey (colour 5) shapes. Every grey shape is a diagonal staircase band. It starts as a horizontal run of width `w` at the top, slides one cell diagonally per row, and ends in a `w×w` square at the bottom. In the output, every grey cell is recoloured using the legend. The legend and the background stay as they are.\n\n**The colouring pattern.** Pair 2 shows it most clearly. Its legend is `1 2 3 8` and its band starts at the top-left corner (4,1). The output paints nested \"L\" shapes:\n- row 4 is `1 1 1 1`;\n- row 5 is `1 2 2 2 2`;\n- row 6 is `1 2 3 3 3 3`;\n- and so on.\n\nEach L has its corner on the diagonal. Its colour is the legend entry at the L's index, cycling through the legend. As a formula: with origin (y0, x0) at the band's starting corner, a cell (y, x) gets index `d = min(y−y0, x−x0)`, and its colour is `legend[d mod n]`.\n\nChecking a few cells from pair 2:\n- (8,2): d = min(4,1) = 1 → colour 2 ✓\n- (8,5): d = 4 → 4 mod 4 = 0 → colour 1 ✓\n\n**The end square.** In the final `w×w` square every cell has the same colour (all 8 in pair 2). The plain formula would give different values there. So `d` must be capped at the index of the last L that fits, which is `cap = shape height − w`.\n- Pair 2: height 15, w = 4, so cap = 11; 11 mod 4 = 3 → colour 8 ✓\n- Pair 1: height 11, w = 3, so cap = 8; 8 mod 3 = 2 → colour 4 ✓\n- Pair 3, first shape: height 9, w = 4, so cap = 5; 5 mod 3 = 2 → colour 3 ✓\n- Pair 3, second shape: height 6, w = 4, so cap = 2 → colour 3 ✓\n\n**`w` is not the legend length.** In pair 3 the band width is 4 but the legend has only 3 colours. So `w` must be measured from the shape itself, as the length of its top row.\n\n**Which way the band runs.** Some bands go down-right, others go down-left. The top row tells them apart:\n- If the top row starts at the bbox's left edge, the origin is the top-left corner and `dx = x − x0` (pair 2, pair 3's first shape).\n- Otherwise the top row ends at the bbox's right edge, the origin is the top-right corner and `dx = x1 − x` (pair 1, pair 3's second shape).\n\n**Test input.** The legend is `1 3 4 2`, so n = 4. There are three grey bands:\n- A down-right band at rows 3–14 with w = 5 and cap = 12 − 5 = 7, so its end square is colour 2.\n- A second down-right band at rows 15–26, identical in shape, also ending in colour 2.\n- A down-left band at rows 1–8 with w = 5 and cap = 3, so its end square is also colour 2.\n\nThe program colours one band at a time and emits the canvas after each band.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    out = g.copy()\n    obs = objects(g, bg=bg)\n    shapes = [o for o in obs if o[\"size\"] > 1]\n    legend_cells = sorted([o for o in obs if o[\"size\"] == 1], key=lambda o: o[\"box\"][1])\n    legend = [o[\"colour\"] for o in legend_cells]\n    n = len(legend)\n    for o in shapes:\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = o[\"box\"]\n        top = sorted(x for (y, x) in o[\"cells\"] if y == y0)\n        w = len(top)\n        left = top[0] == x0\n        cap = (y1 - y0 + 1) - w\n        for (y, x) in o[\"cells\"]:\n            dy = y - y0\n            dx = (x - x0) if left else (x1 - x)\n            d = min(dy, dx, cap)\n            out[y, x] = legend[d % n]\n        emit(out.copy(), f\"Recoloured the band at rows {y0}-{y1} with nested L-shapes cycling through the legend; the end square uses the capped index {cap}.\")\n    emit(out, \"Final grid: every grey band is coloured.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"legend":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"I'll call this the *legend*: for example `1 3 4` or `2 8 3`."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"In the output, every grey cell is recoloured using the legend."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"The legend and the background stay as they are."}],"recolour":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"In the output, every grey cell is recoloured using the legend."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Recoloured the band at rows 3-13 with nested L-shapes cycling through the legend; the end square uses the capped index 8."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Recoloured the band at rows 4-18 with nested L-shapes cycling through the legend; the end square uses the capped index 11."}],"movement":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"It starts as a horizontal run of width `w` at the top, slides one cell diagonally per row, and ends in a `w×w` square at the bottom."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"3ce135ac728947176776251d696ded9130309d53331f559f3553a970accd4649","task_sha256":"561e4ed62fb3db3e672b55b6bde83625143a3fa36a6cb2b38329b646e814f93a","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
